'''''Spathiphyllum wallisii''''', commonly known as '''peace lily''',<ref>{{cite web |title=Spathiphyllum wallisii |url=https://www.gardenersworld.com/plants/spathiphyllum-wallisii/ |publisher=Gardener's World |access-date=21 September 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Ferguson |first1=Donna |title=Houseplants: how to buy them – and keep them alive |url=https://www.theguardian.com/money/2022/mar/12/houseplants-how-to-buy-low-maintenance-plants |access-date=21 September 2023 |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=March 12, 2022}}</ref> '''white sails''',<ref name="modern-gardener">{{cite book |last1=Ellis |first1=Sonya Patel |title=The Modern Gardener: A Practical Guide to Houseplants, Herbs & Container Gardening |date=15 March 2022 |publisher=Simon and Schuster |isbn=978-1-6672-0007-1 |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=ipxhEAAAQBAJ&dq=white+sails+Spathiphyllum+wallisii&pg=PT384 |access-date=21 September 2023 |language=en}}</ref> or '''spathe flower''',<ref>{{cite book |last1=Dehgan |first1=Bijan |title=Garden Plants Taxonomy: Volume 1: Ferns, Gymnosperms, and Angiosperms (Monocots) |date=1 January 2023 |publisher=Springer Nature |isbn=978-3-031-11561-5 |page=223 |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=M9ekEAAAQBAJ |access-date=21 September 2023 |language=en}}</ref> is a very popular indoor [[houseplant|house plant]] of the family [[Araceae]].<ref name="modern-gardener" /> The genus name means "spathe-leaf", and the specific epithet is named after [[Gustav Wallis]], the German [[plant collector]]. It was first described in 1877.

== Description ==
It is a [[herbaceous]] [[perennial plant|perennial]] which produces flowers in the typical aroid structure: a densely crowded [[inflorescence]] called a spadix is subtended by one large [[bract]] called a spathe (occasionally two spathes are produced, with the upper spathe smaller). The [[Spadix (botany)|spadix]] is generally cream or ivory when young, and turns green with age;<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Bercu |first1=R |last2=Făgăraş |first2=M |date=March 2010 |title=Anatomical Aspects of the Ornamental Plant Spathiphyllum wallisii Regel |url=https://pubs.ub.ro/dwnl.php?id=SCSB201018V18S01A0002 |journal=Scientific Study & Research – Biology |volume=18 |pages=13–17 |access-date=6 June 2022}}</ref> the spathe is generally white or white with green nerves distally from the margin, turning green with age. Leaves are basal, glossy and somewhat deeply veined, ovate and acuminate. The petioles are long and the leaves arch gracefully. The plant produces offsets at the base and in time becomes a dense clump.

''Spathiphyllum wallisii'' is one of approximately 40 [[species]] in a genus of [[tropical]] [[evergreens]]. It was discovered in the late 19th century growing wild in [[Colombia]]. A number of cultivars, many of hybrid origin, are commercially available, such as the larger [[Hybrid (biology)|hybrids]] "Mauna Loa", named after the [[Mauna Loa|Hawaiian volcano]], and the even larger “Sensation", which are both popular indoor plants. "Domino" is a finely variegated variety of intermediate size. Its wide natural range includes parts of [[Mexico]], the [[Caribbean Islands]], and northern [[South America]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Spathiphyllum wallisii Regel {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:89011-1 |access-date=26 June 2022 |website=Plants of the World Online |language=en}}</ref>

